      29 +- **International exchange fallback** (implemented): the resolver tries bare                                                                                                                                               \
      30 +  first, then a suffix list driven by input shape. Digits \uc0\u8594  `.HK`, `.TW`,                                                                                                                                                  \
      31 +  `.SS`, `.SZ`, `.T`, `.KS`. Alpha \uc0\u8594  `.L`, `.DE`, `.PA`, `.AS`, `.AX`, `.TO`.                                                                                                                                              \
      32 +  Known edge case: for ambiguous digit codes (e.g. `2330` has both HK and TW                                                                                                                                               \
      33 +  listings), HK wins due to priority order. User can disambiguate by typing                                                                                                                                                \
      34 +  the explicit suffix (`2330.TW`). A future improvement is volume-weighted                                                                                                                                                 \
      35 +  ranking, but it costs an extra Yahoo call per candidate.                                                                                                                                                                 \
