      42 -    missing marker is `pd.NA` don't blow up on `or`-based fallbacks.                                                                 \
      37 +        1. Put/Call ratio z-score vs 20-day history                                                                                  \
      38 +        2. Total Open Interest vs 20-day average                                                                                     \
      39 +        3. Total option volume (calls + puts) vs 20-day average                                                                      \
      40 +        4. IV-HV spread z-score vs full history                                                                                      \
      41 +                                                                                                                                     \
      42 +    Each component's z-score is clipped to \'b13\uc0\u963  and mapped linearly into a                                                            \
      43 +    [0, 100] band, then the four are averaged. This produces an interpretable                                                        \
      44 +    scale where:                                                                                                                     \
      45 +                                                                                                                                     \
      46 +        score == 50   \uc0\u8594  every component is at its own mean (pure neutral)                                                            \
      47 +        score > 50    \uc0\u8594  positioning is above average on net                                                                          \
      48 +        score < 50    \uc0\u8594  positioning is below average on net                                                                          \
      49 +        score == 100  \uc0\u8594  all four components are three standard deviations hot                                                        \
      50 +        score == 0    \uc0\u8594  all four components are three standard deviations cold                                                       \
      51 +                                                                                                                                     \
      52 +    The UI maps this to four honest bands:                                                                                           \
      53 +        <25  calm       \'b7 positioning well below average                                                                             \
      54 +        25-60  normal   \'b7 positioning near the long-term mean                                                                        \
      55 +        60-80  elevated \'b7 above-average positioning, watch for reversal                                                              \
      56 +        >80  crowded    \'b7 extreme consensus, high reversal / squeeze risk                                                            \
      57 +                                                                                                                                     \
      58 +    Note that 62 \uc0\u8776  z-score 0.7 on a single component, or a blend \'97 it is                                                             \
