\uc0\u9210  Auto-Dreaming in Claude \'97 A Blueprint\
\
  Executive summary\
\
  What looks like "dreaming" in an Opus agent is not mystical. It is tightly-coupled feedback between a generation system and a ground-truth source, compressed into a single conversation turn or made persistent via an external scaffold. The generation system is the\
  model's weights plus extended thinking. The ground-truth source is anything that returns a hard "no" \'97 a failing test, a stack trace, a diff, a user correction. Without the ground-truth source, the loop has nothing to push against and collapses into self-reinforcing\
  plausibility within a few iterations. With it, the loop can produce genuine autonomous iteration, idea development, and problem-finding for as long as budget allows. This document is the blueprint.\
