      127 +| Platform | Default path |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
      128 +|---|---|                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
      129 +| macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/VolScope/volscope.db` |                                                                                                                                                                                            \
      130 +| Linux | `$XDG_DATA_HOME/volscope/volscope.db` (or `~/.local/share/volscope/...`) |                                                                                                                                                                        \
      131 +| Override | Set `VOLSCOPE_DATA_DIR=/some/path` in `.env` or the shell. |                                                                                                                                                                                   \
      132  \
      133 +The DB location is outside the project directory on purpose: macOS `fileprovi`                                                                                                                                                                              \
      134 +(iCloud File Provider) grabs write handles on anything under `~/Desktop`,                                                                                                                                                                                   \
      135 +which collides with DuckDB's exclusive lock. Keeping the DB in                                                                                                                                                                                              \
      136 +Application Support avoids that.                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \
      137 +                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \
      138 +## Troubleshooting                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
      139 +                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \
      140 +**"Legacy seed data detected" banner on Scope.** Your DB has rows from a                                                                                                                                                                                    \
      141 +pre-v1.0 seed where `iv_30d == hv_20d` (flat zero spread). Click the                                                                                                                                                                                        \
      142 +**Fix now** button in the banner, or **Fix all tickers** for a full                                                                                                                                                                                         \
      143 +migration. No CLI / restart needed.                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \
      144 +                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \
      145 +**"Database unavailable" on startup.** Another VolScope process is holding                                                                                                                                                                                  \
      146 +the DuckDB write lock. Usually a stale `streamlit run` or a running                                                                                                                                                                                         \
      147 +`make scrape`. Stop it and reload.                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
      148 +                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \
      149 +**SPY IV looks wrong (> 50%).** An old scraper run with broken ATM                                                                                                                                                                                          \
      150 +interpolation. The scrape sanity layer now rejects IV > 120% for broad ETFs                                                                                                                                                                                 \
      151 +and > 500% for single names. Run `make scrape` once and the stale row gets                                                                                                                                                                                  \
      152 +overwritten with the corrected value.                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \
